<title>RUSSIA: Russia to auction 20 trln rbls June 18.</title>
<headline>Russia to auction 20 trln rbls June 18.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's Finance Ministry will offer 20 trillion roubles -- the largest sum ever sold in one day's auctions -- of GKO discount Treasury bills and OFZ interest-bearing bonds at auctions on June 18, the Central Bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:  </p>
<p>Full details of the T-bill auction:</p>
<p>    Series number		    21076</p>
<p>    Issue volume		     8.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		    1.00 million</p>
<p>    Issue date			 June 18, 1997</p>
<p>    Tenor				364 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		    June 17, 1998</p>
<p>    Full details of the bond auction:</p>
<p>    Series number		    24014</p>
<p>    Issue volume		     12 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		    1.00 million</p>
<p>    Issue date			 June 18, 1997</p>
<p>    Tenor				728 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		    June 16, 1999</p>
<p>    First coupon rate		19.73 pct</p>
<p>    First coupon date		December 17, 1997</p>
<p>    Second coupon date	     June 17, 1998</p>
<p>    Third coupon date		December 16, 1998</p>
<p>    Fourth coupon date	     June 16, 1999</p>
<p>On June 18 the Finance Ministry will also repay about 7.12 trillion roubles in a maturing issue of 245-day T-bills (series 22054) and pay 1.25 trillion roubles in interest on the series 24010 OFZ bond maturing in June 1998.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
